,"guid":"da52796f-2621-3351-8e77-955da92ea82d","description":"UEFA Champions League","sportId":600,"leagueId":2,"league":{"id":775,"description":"UEFA Champions League","abbreviation":"UEFA Champions League","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/uefa.champions"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/uefa.champions"}}}}},{"type":"event","uid":"s:600~l:775~e:401915312","guid":"da2a9bc8-370a-3a04-9098-45e1191c5d6f","description":"Arsenal @ Bayern Munich","eventId":401915312,"event":{"id":401915312,"sport":"soccer","league":"uefa.champions","description":"Arsenal @ Bayern Munich"}}],"ad":{"bundle":"espnfc","sport":"Soccer"},"tracking":{"coverageType":"Analysis","leagueName":"UEFA Champions League","program":"EPSN","sportName":"soccer","trackingId":"dm_261021_COM_SOC_Analysis_Klinsmann3A_Draw_damages_Bayern_Munich_more_than_Arsenal__GLOBAL_2026-10-21","trackingName":"COM_SOC Analysis (Klinsmann: Draw damages Bayern Munich more than Arsenal ) GLOBAL 2026-10-21"}}],"categories":[{"id":81497,"type":"league","uid":"s:600","guid":"119cfa41-71d4-39bf-a790-6273a52b0259","description":"Soccer","sportId":600,"leagueId":600,"league":{"id":600,"description":"Soccer","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/"}}}}},{"id":270401,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:600~a:218522","guid":"c33411df-3312-09c1-662b-0097aa3a7e72","description":"Bruno Guimarães","sportId":600,"athleteId":218522,"athlete":{"id":218522,"description":"Bruno Guimarães","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/218522/bruno-guimaraes"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/218522/bruno-guimaraes"}}}}},{"id":142299,"type":"team","uid":"s:600~t:359","guid":"feb44e87-58fa-9597-2691-b3c32768ebe4","description":"Arsenal","sportId":600,"teamId":359,"team":{"id":359,"description":"Arsenal","abbreviation":"ARS","shortDisplayName":"Arsenal","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/club/_/id/359/arsenal"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/club/_/id/359/arsenal"}}}}},{"id":142294,"type":"team","uid":"s:600~t:361","guid":"ec6b4352-98d3-424d-6214-778d79b47a01","description":"Newcastle United","sportId":600,"teamId":361,"team":{"id":361,"description":"Newcastle United","abbreviation":"NEW","shortDisplayName":"Newcastle","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/club/_/id/361/newcastle-united"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/club/_/id/361/newcastle-united"}}}}},{"id":137781,"type":"league","uid":"s:600~l:700","guid":"6949f3af-300c-35f1-beab-b95669eedd38","description":"English Premier League","sportId":600,"leagueId":23,"league":{"id":700,"description":"English Premier League","abbreviation":"Premier League","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/eng.1"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/eng.1"}}}}},{"id":518441,"type":"topic","guid":"c20f7f80-f88e-4084-6567-d1bf00c52bf0","description":"soccer transfers","sportId":0,"topicId":3},{"id":696285,"type":"contributor","guid":"a1a120f9-cadb-3124-93ed-c3f8c7ac3a6b","description":"James Olley","slug":"james-olley","contributor":{"id":3853,"description":"James Olley"}}],"keywords":["Soccer","Bruno Guimarães","Arsenal","Newcastle United","English Premier League","soccer transfers","James Olley"],"story":"<p><a data-player-guid=\"c33411df-3312-09c1-662b-0097aa3a7e72\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/218522/bruno-guimaraes\">Bruno Guimarães</a> has admitted he had sleepless nights over his decision to leave <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"ec6b4352-98d3-424d-6214-778d79b47a01\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=361\">Newcastle United</a> for <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"feb44e87-58fa-9597-2691-b3c32768ebe4\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=359\">Arsenal</a>.</p>\n<p>The 28-year-old spent four years at St James' Park, becoming captain in 2024 before moving to the Gunners for £75 million ($100 million) in the summer.</p>\n<p>Newcastle sporting director Ross Wilson said at the time that the club had no wish to sell Guimarães during a turbulent transfer window -- in which several players including <a data-player-guid=\"1c67a47d-7b8f-d560-6aaf-0f9e73b00f51\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/268782/anthony-gordon\">Anthony Gordon</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"760d112b-ec65-40cb-e513-e7a3b0c2448d\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/player/_/id/261047/sandro-tonali\">Sandro Tonali</a> were sold while manager Eddie Howe also departed -- but the midfielder pushed to leave.</p>\n<p>Guimarães released a statement claiming it was \"one of the toughest decisions of my life\" and opened up about the transfer when speaking to reporters following Arsenal's 2-2 draw at <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"25b5e432-d3d2-939f-f73b-6e531a6fbd91\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=132\">Bayern Munich</a> on Wednesday.</p>\n<p><photo caption=\"Bruno Guimarães moved to Arsenal after four years on Tyneside.\"></p>\n<p>\"It was very difficult for me because I had an amazing relationship with everyone at Newcastle,\" said Guimarães, who lifted the club's first domestic trophy in 70 years when Newcastle beat <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"a47fbcec-c948-cf4c-9e41-3dfa37588c9c\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=364\">Liverpool</a> in the 2025 <a data-league-guid=\"7d7df547-a8c6-37a7-947d-7b661c801ff5\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/soccer/league/_/name/ENG.LEAGUE_CUP\">Carabao Cup</a> Final.</p>\n<p>\"I did my best for the club. I think I was there for almost five years and inside of me, I just wanted a new challenge. To be fair, it was very tough for me to make this decision because I really enjoyed my time at the club, the affection I had for the fans.</p>\n<p>\"So, it was a difficult one. I lost many, many nights of sleep because it was difficult for me, for my family. But now I am here, I am just trying to give my best for Arsenal.</p>\n<p>\"I think I did great for Newcastle. We won a trophy after 70 years. We got into the Champions League twice. We got to two finals. I think I did what I could for the club. I wish them all the best because they were so nice to me. It is just time to move on. I have been enjoying my time here at Arsenal as well.\"</p>\n<p>Guimarães had formed a close bond with Newcastle supporters and Howe and the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"2a051c42-4444-8263-799a-6cdd866bd8f7\" href=\"http://espn.com/soccer/team?id=205\">Brazil</a> international continued: \"It was not just hard to tell Eddie, but to tell the owners, my team-mates. But I think the club went to a new rotation, a lot of players left as well. The gaffer left as well. It was tough, because my connection with the club was unbelievable.</p>\n<p>\"I never felt so loved like the way I was at Newcastle. I hope I can have the same love here at Arsenal, but the connection I had was unbelievable. It was hard for me to say bye to them. I remember, when I said bye to the lads, I was crying. They were crying as well, because we were a family there.\"</p>\n<p><strong>- <a href=\"https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/50241594/star-attackers-not-needed-arsenal-win-champions-league\" target=\"_blank\">Star attackers might not be needed for Arsenal to win Champions League</a><br>\n- <a href=\"https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/50240494/saka-limps-10th-minute-arsenal-match-bayern\" target=\"_blank\">Saka forced off after 'sharp pain;' Arteta says 'doesn't look good'</a><br>\n- <a href=\"https://www.espn.co.uk/football/story/_/id/50230051/newcastle-aston-villa-botman-jackson-tackle-var-webb\" target=\"_blank\">Referees' boss Webb backs VAR over Newcastle's Botman challenge on Villa's Jackson</a></strong></p>\n<p>Guimarães endured a slow start at Arsenal due to a nagging groin injury but he has now made 13 appearances so far and started back-to-back Champions League games for the first time in Munich.</p>\n<p>Many Arsenal players speak about Mikel Arteta's meticulous attention to detail and Guimarães added: \"We always want to win. That is the mentality that we go to the training ground with every day.</p>\n<p>\"He [Arteta] is always a little bit addicted to videos and the way that he can make us feel better on the pitch. I think we have a top manager with a top mentality. We want to win everything possible.\"</p>\n<p><inline1></p>\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"byline":"James Olley","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50247830"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50247830"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/soccer/story?storyId=50247830"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/50247830/bruno-guimaraes-sleepless-nights-arsenal-move"}},"premium":false}],"breakingNews":[],"timestamp":"2026-10-22T23:07:22Z","status":"success"}